Description: import scans from a scanner's memory as searchable PDFs
 Flypage notices when a scanner with internal memory (such as an IRIScan
 Book) is plugged in, copies its files and opens a window where the scans
 are sorted into named folders by drag and drop. Each document is turned
 into a PDF with an invisible OCR text layer, so it can be searched and its
 text copied.
 .
 Each scan gives its own PDF, output files are named from a template, and
 scans can be moved (deleted from the scanner once their PDF is written) or
 copied. OCR uses Tesseract through ocrmypdf; PNG, JPEG and PDF files are
 accepted, and images can also be filed as they are, without OCR.
